From: Yuzhi Zhu <explodingtnt@foxmail.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Nov 2026 13:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 21/21] hp39gii: SmartFS partition layout, NCB backup repair,
 boot counter

The board bring-up ends here: the NAND is partitioned so that everything
below block 238 (the stock firmware area) is never touched, blocks
245..1023 carry a 97 MB SmartFS volume, and block 4 -- the second copy of
the stock NCB -- is repaired from block 0 if an earlier, wrong
mtd_partition() call erased it.

mtd_partition() takes its arguments in read/write blocks (pages here), not
erase blocks; passing erase blocks put the partition on top of block 4.
The repair path is the fix for the units.

Also adds a boot counter in /mnt/boot.txt so that a written-then-read-back
value proves the file really reached NAND instead of staying in cache.
---
 boards/arm/stmp3770/hp39gii/configs/nsh/defconfig  |   2 +
 boards/arm/stmp3770/hp39gii/src/hp39gii_boot.c     | 326 +++++++++++++++-------
 arch/arm/src/stmp3770/stmp3770_mtd.c               |  23 ++-
 3 files changed, 262 insertions(+), 89 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/src/stmp3770/stmp3770_mtd.c b/arch/arm/src/stmp3770/stmp3770_mtd.c
